# @title Tabs - Smoke
# Visits every bottom tab once and checks each one renders its own content, so a tab whose screen crashes or
# whose query fails shows up here. Read-only: it doesn't change the test account.
# Tab screens stay mounted after their first visit, and Android keeps them in the accessibility tree, so each
# wait is for something only that tab renders, and each tab is visited once. Home's search-button is still in the
# tree on later tabs, so it only proves Home rendered at launch.
# @launch useE2EInit=true email=${EMAIL} password=${PASSWORD}
open ${APP_ID}
# The first launch on a cold CI simulator can take over a minute
wait 'id="search-button"' 90000
# Tabs are pressed by testID (tabBarButtonTestID): on Android, label="Search" also matches Home's search button
press 'id="bottom-tab-search"'
wait 'label="Explore by Category" || text="Explore by Category"' 30000
press 'id="bottom-tab-inbox"'
wait 'label="Inquiries" || text="Inquiries"' 30000
press 'id="bottom-tab-favorites"'
wait 'label="Learn more about Favorites"' 30000
press 'id="bottom-tab-profile"'
wait 'id="account-card"' 30000
